            We ranked these on the label and on public information, not on hands-on taste tests: how much of the protein comes from rice, protein per serving, calories, sweeteners, third-party testing and any heavy-metal data, plus price tier at the time of writing. Our <a href="/how-we-test/">how we test</a> page explains the method. Nutrition figures are per the label or brand listing and vary by flavor. The first three picks are rice-only. The rest are blends where brown rice protein is one of the two main sources, because that is where most buyers end up once they understand the amino acid trade-off.
          </p>

